-- title:
--   Cotangent functional vanishing on the relaxation kernel
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal O$ be a complete discrete valuation ring (a domain, complete for its maximal-adic topology), let $\bar\rho$ be a two-dimensional residual Galois representation over the residue field of $\mathcal O$, and let $\mathcal D_0$, $\mathcal D'$ be two deformation conditions, i.e. predicates on adically continuous rank-two Galois representations over local $\mathcal O$-algebras. Let $D_0$ and $D'$ be `DeformationRingData` for $\bar\rho$ and these conditions, so each consists of a complete Noetherian local $\mathcal O$-algebra $R$ with residue field generated by that of $\mathcal O$, a representation $\rho$ over $R$ of the given type whose residual representation is equivalent to the base change of $\bar\rho$, together with the universal property that every such deformation over a complete Noetherian local $\mathcal O$-algebra arises from a unique local $\mathcal O$-algebra map out of $R$. Let $\theta : R' \to R_0$ be a surjective local $\mathcal O$-algebra map with $\theta_*\rho'$ equivalent to $\rho_0$, let $x_0 : R_0 \to \mathcal O$ be an $\mathcal O$-algebra map, and write $I = \ker(x_0 \circ \theta)$. Let $S$ be an $\mathcal O$-algebra whose trivial square-zero extension $S[\varepsilon] = S \oplus S\varepsilon$ is local, Noetherian, adically complete, with $\mathcal O \to S[\varepsilon]$ local and surjective onto the residue field. Let $\varphi : I/I^2 \to S$ be $\mathcal O$-linear and let $\psi : R' \to S[\varepsilon]$ be a local $\mathcal O$-algebra map whose $\varepsilon$-component on $I$ is given by $\varphi$ composed with $I \to I/I^2$; no condition is imposed on the first component of $\psi$. Assume the base change $\psi_*\rho'$ satisfies both $\mathcal D'$ and $\mathcal D_0$. Then $\varphi$ vanishes on the kernel of the induced map $I/I^2 \to \ker(x_0)/\ker(x_0)^2$ coming from $\theta$; precisely, $\varphi$ composed with the inclusion of that kernel is the zero map.
--
--   This is the step in Mazur's cotangent-space analysis which shows that a functional on the relative cotangent space of the larger (relaxed) deformation problem, realised by a square-zero lift that happens to be of the smaller type, descends to the cotangent space of the smaller problem. It is used in the rungs of the numerical criterion comparing deformation rings, and is cited by [`GaloisRep.DeformationRingData.exists_localInvariant_of_ordinaryLine`](thm.html#GaloisRep.DeformationRingData.exists_localInvariant_of_ordinaryLine).
